 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "<p>“Approaching a party who were eating their breakfast, I got to speak with them. They asked me to have some breakfast with them . . . During the meal I got a chance to ask them many questions. They proved to be a Texas outfit, who had just come up with a herd of cattle and having delivered them they were preparing to return. There were several colored cow boys among them, and good ones too. After breakfast I asked the camp boss for a job as cow boy. . . . So he spoke to one of the colored cow boys called Bronko Jim, and told him to go out and rope old Good Eye, saddle him and put me on his back. Bronko Jim gave me a few pointers . . . I told Jim I was a good rider and not afraid of him. I thought I had rode pitching horses before, but from the time I mounted old Good Eye I knew I had not learned what pitching was. This proved the worst horse to ride I had ever mounted in my life, but I stayed with him . . . After the horse got tired and I dismounted the boss said he would give me a job and pay me $30.00 per month and more later on. He asked what my name was and I answered Nat Love”</p>\n<p align=\"right\">Nat Love, <i>The Life and Adventures of Nat Love</i>, 1907</p>\n<p><i>Refer to the excerpt provided.</i></p>",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 615687,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Freedman Nat Love’s being asked to join the group of “cow boys” signals what development in the identity of the American West?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1170717,
     "content_html": "Workers were hired based on their skills, not necessarily their race."
    },
    {
     "id": 1170716,
     "content_html": "Cattle owners were in need of workers, regardless of their skills."
    },
    {
     "id": 1170715,
     "content_html": "The West was populated by segregationists."
    },
    {
     "id": 1170714,
     "content_html": "Cattle owners discriminated only against American Indians."
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 615688,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Events such as those depicted in the excerpt demonstrated that the American West was a region where",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1170721,
     "content_html": "“rugged individualism” was prevalent"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170720,
     "content_html": "equal opportunity was not widespread"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170719,
     "content_html": "Civil War attitudes toward race remained"
    },
    {
     "id": 1170718,
     "content_html": "the Cattle Kingdom attracted only white men"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "multiple-choice"
   ],
   "combo_choices": []
  },
  {
   "id": 615689,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Which development contextualizes the situation described in the excerpt?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1170724,
     "content_html": "Industrialization drove people out of the cities into the American West."
    },
    {
     "id": 1170723,
     "content_html": "Immigration resulted in overpopulation of the eastern cities, forcing people to look for employment elsewhere."
    },
    {
     "id": 1170725,
     "content_html": "The West provided opportunity for those who were willing to take a risk."
    },
    {
     "id": 1170722,
     "content_html": "People shut out of the wealth made in the Gilded Age were forced out of the major cities."
    }
   ],
